<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR firmer as peso rates rise.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR firmer as peso rates rise.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) rose across the board on Tuesday following the increase in the overnight rates, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;The PHIBOR are just reflecting the movement in the peso rates,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>The Manila interbank call loan rate went up after the Central Bank raised its overnight borrowing and lending rates.</p>
<p>PHIBOR are average foreign exchange forward rates quoted by 20 banks operating in the country.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			 Sept 3		  Sept 2</p>
<p>    1 W		12  3/8		 10 3/4</p>
<p>    2 W		12  1/4		 10 7/8</p>
<p>    1 M		11 15/16		10 7/8</p>
<p>    2 M		11  5/8		 11</p>
<p>    3 M		11  5/8		 11 1/16</p>
<p>    6 M		11 13/16		11 3/8</p>
<p>    12M		11 15/16		11 3/4</p>
<p>    VAL		4-Sep		   3-Sep</p>
<p>--Manila newsroom (632) 841-89-36, fax 817-62-67</p>
